    "summary": "Model completed and passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nBridge: single simply-supported span, 25 m centre-to-centre of bearings, deck width 16 m. Five precast prestressed small-box girders per span (C40), middle-girder section depth 1.4 m, top width 2.40 m; single-girder A = 1.0605 m², I = 0.25166 m⁴; girder Ec = 32 500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³, total self-weight w = 137.87 kN/m, mass m = 14.05 t/m. Supports: abutments at both ends on plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×350 mm, 4×8 mm layers, Ge = 1.0 MPa default), 2 per girder end → 10 per line; modelled as zero-length springs with Kv = 1.416×10⁷ kN/m, Kh = 3.281×10⁴ kN/m, rotation free. Live load: Highway Class II (JTG D60-2015), one-way, 4 design lanes; qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 232.5 kN, ξ = 0.67; impact factor μ = 0.241 from f1 = 4.272 Hz.\n\nRoot cause of the earlier failure (L2-1): the accepted lane.qk was 10.5 kN/m, i.e. the Class I value without the Class II 0.75 reduction. The code clause JTGD60-4.3.1-qk recomputes qk = 10.5 × 0.75 = 7.875 kN/m for load_class II; the model's parameter therefore disagreed with its governing clause. Revising lane.qk to 7.875 kN/m (evidence JTGD60-4.3.1-qk, INPUT:deck.load_class) and regenerating fixed it.\n\nKey results: first vertical frequency 4.272 Hz (next modes 16.90, 37.30 Hz); self-weight support reactions 1723.3 kN each; self-weight midspan moment 10 771 kNm; governing live-load (lane) positive moment 6878 kNm, no negative lane moment."
